LOK: .uno:SlideObjects says whether the marked object's text is being edited

A client that must unmark the objects for a command (Impress narrows
Replace All to the marked ones) restores the marks afterwards, and
the text edit that unmarking ended. It knew of the edit only by the
caret the kit had told it; the caret callback comes after the paint
that follows entering the edit, so a command arriving in between
found no caret, restored the marks alone, and the keys typed next
went nowhere (Ely R18.8: a box entered as its tab finished loading,
another program's replace 170 ms later).
The selection now carries "editing", read in the same call that
lists the marks.
--- a/sd/source/ui/unoidl/unomodel.cxx
+++ b/sd/source/ui/unoidl/unomodel.cxx
@@ -2180,6 +2180,8 @@
     rJson.put("kind", aKind);
     rJson.put("canGroup", rView.IsGroupPossible());
     rJson.put("canUngroup", rView.IsUnGroupPossible());
+    // Ely: a caret told later is not yet known.
+    rJson.put("editing", rView.IsTextEdit());
     const SfxItemSet aAttr(rView.GetAttrFromMarked(false));
     rJson.put("fill", lcl_Color(aAttr, XATTR_FILLSTYLE, XATTR_FILLCOLOR, false));
     rJson.put("line", lcl_Color(aAttr, XATTR_LINESTYLE, XATTR_LINECOLOR, true));
